{
  "schemaVersion": 7,
  "description": "ALT TABAN (bottom sheet): a flat circular sheet disc of outer diameter A and thickness F, lying in the XY plane with its flat back face at z=0 and its centre on the Z axis. It has a central through bore of diameter D. Four through holes of diameter C sit on a pitch circle of diameter B at 0/90/180/270 degrees. Each hole has a raised round collar of height E on the \u002BZ face, which is the face seen in the plan view and the isometric view. Two identical radial U-notches (width 14, radius 7, depth 16.5 from the outer edge, green construction dimensions) are cut from the outer edge at 45 and 225 degrees. Section A-A runs along the Y axis at x=0 and passes through the top and bottom holes. Collar outer diameter is estimated from the proportional section and plan views because it is not dimensioned. Column H is not a measurement; the output ID is used for the title block only.",
